      "kind": "input",
      "refersTo": "input-field",
      "description": "Borderless silver field; focus is a 2px inset sky-text stroke.",
      "html": "<input class=\"ds-field\" placeholder=\"Body weight (kg)\">",
      "css": ".ds-field{font-family:var(--font,'Archivo Variable','Archivo',system-ui,sans-serif);width:100%;background:var(--surface,#eef2f6);color:var(--label,#13233f);border:none;border-radius:var(--r,4px);padding:13px 15px;font-size:17px;outline:none;transition:box-shadow 140ms}.ds-field::placeholder{color:var(--label-3,rgba(19,35,63,.66))}.ds-field:focus,.ds-field:focus-visible{box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 2px var(--acc-text,#1468ad)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Chips",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "chip",
      "description": "Silver 4px chips; the selected chip is a navy ink fill.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-chips\"><button class=\"ds-chip ds-on\">All</button><button class=\"ds-chip\">Back</button><button class=\"ds-chip\">Legs</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-chips{display:flex;gap:7px}.ds-chip{font-family:var(--font,'Archivo Variable','Archivo',system-ui,sans-serif);padding:6px 13px;border:none;border-radius:var(--r,4px);background:var(--surface,#eef2f6);color:var(--label,#13233f);font-size:14px;cursor:pointer;transition:background 140ms,color 140ms}.ds-chip:hover,.ds-chip:active{background:var(--surface-2,#e2e8ef)}.ds-chip.ds-on{background:var(--ink,#13233f);color:var(--bg,#fff);font-weight:600}.ds-chip:focus-visible{outline:2.5px solid var(--acc-text,#1468ad);outline-offset:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Week Strip",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "week-day-today",
      "description": "Seven columns: uppercase weekday, condensed date, square status dot; today is a navy square.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-week\"><div class=\"ds-wday\"><div class=\"ds-lbl\">Mo</div><div class=\"ds-num\">5</div><div class=\"ds-dot ds-done\"></div></div><div class=\"ds-wday ds-today\"><div class=\"ds-lbl\">Tu</div><div class=\"ds-num\">6</div><div class=\"ds-dot ds-ovr\"></div></div><div class=\"ds-wday\"><div class=\"ds-lbl\">We</div><div class=\"ds-num\">7</div><div class=\"ds-dot ds-plan\"></div></div><div class=\"ds-wday\"><div class=\"ds-lbl\">Th</div><div class=\"ds-num\">8</div><div class=\"ds-dot\"></div></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-week{font-family:var(--font,'Archivo Variable','Archivo',system-ui,sans-serif);display:flex;gap:4px;background:var(--surface,#eef2f6);border-radius:var(--r,4px);padding:12px;color:var(--label,#13233f)}.ds-wday{flex:1;text-align:center;padding:8px 2px 9px;border-radius:var(--r,4px)}.ds-wday:active{background:var(--surface-2,#e2e8ef)}.ds-lbl{font-size:11px;font-weight:600;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;color:var(--label-2,rgba(19,35,63,.7))}.ds-num{font-size:19px;font-weight:600;font-stretch:78%;margin:4px 0}.ds-today .ds-num{background:var(--ink,#13233f);color:var(--bg,#fff);font-weight:700;width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:var(--r,4px);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin:2px auto}.ds-dot{width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:1px;margin:0 auto}.ds-dot.ds-plan{background:var(--label-4,rgba(19,35,63,.2))}.ds-dot.ds-done{background:var(--ink,#13233f)}.ds-dot.ds-ovr{box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1.5px var(--ink,#13233f)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tab Bar",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "tab-start",
      "description": "Solid bottom bar with hairline top; active tab gets a 3px sky bar; Start is a raised 54px sky square, and while a session runs it stays sky with a 3px inset ink bar on top (no ping).",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-tabbar\"><button class=\"ds-tab ds-on\"><svg width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.1\" stroke-linecap=\"square\" stroke-linejoin=\"miter\"><path d=\"M3 11l9-7 9 7v10H3z\"/></svg>Home</button><button class=\"ds-tab\"><svg width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.7\" stroke-linecap=\"square\" stroke-linejoin=\"miter\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"5\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\"/><path d=\"M3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4\"/></svg>Plan</button><button class=\"ds-tab ds-start ds-rec\"><span class=\"ds-cir\"><svg width=\"26\" height=\"26\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"square\" stroke-linejoin=\"miter\"><path d=\"M6 8v8M9 6v12M15 6v12M18 8v8M9 12h6\"/></svg></span><span>Start</span></button><button class=\"ds-tab\"><svg width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.7\" stroke-linecap=\"square\" stroke-linejoin=\"miter\"><path d=\"M5 20V12M10 20V6M15 20v-9M20 20V9\"/></svg>Progress</button></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-tabbar{font-family:var(--font,'Archivo Variable','Archivo',system-ui,sans-serif);display:flex;justify-content:space-around;align-items:flex-end;padding:7px 6px 6px;background:var(--bg-el,#fff);border-top:1px solid var(--sep,rgba(19,35,63,.16))}.ds-tab{font-family:var(--font,'Archivo Variable','Archivo',system-ui,sans-serif);flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:3px;padding-top:5px;position:relative;border:none;background:none;color:var(--label-2,rgba(19,35,63,.7));font-size:11px;font-weight:500;cursor:pointer;transition:color 140ms}.ds-tab:hover{color:var(--label,#13233f)}.ds-tab:focus-visible{outline:2.5px solid var(--acc-text,#1468ad);outline-offset:2px}.ds-tab.ds-on{color:var(--label,#13233f);font-weight:650}.ds-tab.ds-on::before{content:'';position:absolute;top:-7px;width:28px;height:3px;background:var(--acc,#3a9fe4)}.ds-start{margin-top:-24px;color:var(--label,#13233f);font-weight:650}.ds-cir{width:54px;height:54px;border-radius:var(--r,4px);background:var(--d-train,#3a9fe4);color:var(--on-field,#13233f);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;transition:transform 140ms cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1)}.ds-start:active .ds-cir{transform:scale(.93)}.ds-start.ds-rec .ds-cir{box-shadow:inset 0 3px 0 var(--ink,#13233f)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Toast",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "toast",
      "description": "Solid navy ink bar with a 4px corner; never a pill.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-toast\">Weight saved</div>",
      "css": ".ds-toast{font-family:var(--font,'Archivo Variable','Archivo',system-ui,sans-serif);display:inline-block;background:var(--ink,#13233f);color:var(--bg,#fff);border-radius:var(--r,4px);padding:11px 18px;font-size:15px;font-weight:500;max-width:88vw}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Plan Day Rows",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "plan-day-square",
      "description": "Weekday rows led by a 56px square with the two-letter weekday: sky for training days, rest silver for rest days.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-plist\"><div class=\"ds-pday ds-on\"><span class=\"ds-psq\">Mo</span><span class=\"ds-pt\">Monday</span></div><div class=\"ds-pday\"><span class=\"ds-psq\">Tu</span><span class=\"ds-pt\">Tuesday</span><span class=\"ds-tag\">Rest</span></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-plist{font-family:var(--font,'Archivo Variable','Archivo',system-ui,sans-serif);display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1px;background:var(--sep,rgba(19,35,63,.16));border-radius:var(--r,4px);overflow:hidden;color:var(--label,#13233f)}.ds-pday{display:flex;align-items:stretch;gap:14px;min-height:56px;background:var(--surface,#eef2f6);padding-inline-end:12px}.ds-psq{width:56px;flex:none;display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:17px;font-weight:700;font-stretch:112%;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em;background:var(--d-rest,#c4ccd5);color:var(--on-field,#13233f)}.ds-pday.ds-on .ds-psq{background:var(--d-train,#3a9fe4)}.ds-pt{align-self:center;flex:1;font-size:17px;font-weight:650}.ds-pday:not(.ds-on) .ds-pt{color:var(--label-2,rgba(19,35,63,.7))}.ds-tag{align-self:center;background:var(--surface-2,#e2e8ef);color:var(--label-2,rgba(19,35,63,.7));border-radius:3px;padding:3px 7px;font-size:12px;font-weight:500}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Coach Entry",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "coach-band-square",
      "description": "Silver band led by a full-height 64px ink square.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-coach\"><span class=\"ds-coach-sq\">AI</span><span class=\"ds-coach-t\"><b>Coach</b><span>Build a plan with the coach</span></span></button>",
      "css": ".ds-coach{font-family:var(--font,'Archivo Variable','Archivo',system-ui,sans-serif);display:flex;align-items:stretch;width:100%;text-align:start;padding:0;border:none;border-radius:var(--r,4px);overflow:hidden;background:var(--surface,#eef2f6);color:var(--label,#13233f);cursor:pointer;transition:background 140ms}.ds-coach:active,.ds-coach:hover{background:var(--surface-2,#e2e8ef)}.ds-coach-sq{width:64px;flex:none;display:grid;place-items:center;background:var(--ink,#13233f);color:var(--bg,#fff);font-weight:700}.ds-coach-t{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;padding:13px 14px}.ds-coach-t b{font-size:17px;font-weight:700;font-stretch:112%}.ds-coach-t span{font-size:13px;color:var(--label-2,rgba(19,35,63,.7))}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Stats Tile and PR Badge",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "stat-tile",
      "description": "Silver tile with a 4px domain stripe, wide uppercase label and 36px condensed numeral; PR badge as a solid yellow field with navy ink.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-tiles\"><div class=\"ds-tile\"><div class=\"ds-tl\">Workouts</div><div class=\"ds-tv\">128</div></div><div class=\"ds-tile ds-body\"><div class=\"ds-tl\">Weight 30d</div><div class=\"ds-tv\">−1.4 kg</div></div></div><span class=\"ds-pr\">PR</span>",
      "css": ".ds-tiles{font-family:var(--font,'Archivo Variable','Archivo',system-ui,sans-serif);display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:10px;margin-bottom:10px;color:var(--label,#13233f)}.ds-tile{background:var(--surface,#eef2f6);border-radius:var(--r,4px);padding:16px 14px 14px;box-shadow:inset 0 4px 0 var(--tile-f,var(--d-train,#3a9fe4))}.ds-tile.ds-body{--tile-f:var(--d-body,#34b06a)}.ds-tl{font-size:12px;font-weight:700;font-stretch:112%;letter-spacing:.05em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--label-2,rgba(19,35,63,.7))}.ds-tv{font-size:36px;font-weight:700;font-stretch:78%;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;letter-spacing:-.01em;margin-top:6px;line-height:1}.ds-pr{font-family:var(--font,'Archivo Variable','Archivo',system-ui,sans-serif);display:inline-flex;background:var(--d-move,#f5c932);color:var(--on-field,#13233f);border-radius:3px;padding:3px 8px;font-size:12px;font-weight:700}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Set Rows",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "set-number-next",
      "description": "Set-number squares: silver by default, sky for the next set, green when done; condensed tabular values.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-sets\"><div class=\"ds-set\"><span class=\"ds-n ds-done\">1</span><span class=\"ds-v\">80 kg × 8</span><span class=\"ds-ck ds-on\">✓</span></div><div class=\"ds-set\"><span class=\"ds-n ds-next\">2</span><span class=\"ds-v\">80 kg × 8</span><span class=\"ds-ck\"></span></div><div class=\"ds-set\"><span class=\"ds-n\">3</span><span class=\"ds-v\">80 kg × 8</span><span class=\"ds-ck\"></span></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-sets{font-family:var(--font,'Archivo Variable','Archivo',system-ui,sans-serif);display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;color:var(--label,#13233f)}.ds-set{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px}.ds-n{width:26px;height:26px;border-radius:3px;background:var(--surface-2,#e2e8ef);display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;font-stretch:78%}.ds-n.ds-next{background:var(--d-train,#3a9fe4);color:var(--on-field,#13233f)}.ds-n.ds-done{background:var(--d-body,#34b06a);color:var(--on-field,#13233f)}.ds-v{flex:1;font-size:17px;font-stretch:78%;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-ck{width:30px;height:30px;border-radius:3px;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 2px var(--label-2,rgba(19,35,63,.7));display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:16px;font-weight:700}.ds-ck.ds-on{background:var(--d-body,#34b06a);box-shadow:none;color:var(--on-field,#13233f)}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Games Programme",
    "overview": "SuperOpenGym is drawn as a sports identity system in the Munich '72 tradition of Otl Aicher. Each domain of a cut (training, body, nutrition, activity, strength) owns one flat colour, and that colour arrives as a whole field, never as a sprinkle. You know where you are from the colour before you read a word. The numerals report the state, and every field has one job, done with one tap on the ink bar at its foot.\n\nThe ground is white in light mode (the default, chosen for bright gyms and daylight) and deep navy in dark mode. Ink is a deep navy, never black. Silver carries rest, structure and every neutral grouping. One grotesque family, Archivo, does all the typographic work through its width axis: wide capitals for headings and routine names, condensed tabular figures for the big numbers, and normal width for reading. Corners are a small 4px everywhere. Surfaces are flat, layout is built from colour fields, silver tone steps and hairline rules, and nothing floats.\n\nDensity is calm rather than sparse. One field leads the first viewport, then stacked full-width bands each carry one key number. Motion is straight and short. Fields travel on straight paths in 200–260ms with an ease-out, and numerals never bounce or count up.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Five fixed domain colours used as whole fields, plus silver for rest.",
      "Navy ink in both themes. Ink on any coloured field is always navy.",
      "One family, Archivo Variable, with its width axis as the type grid (wide 112, condensed 78).",
      "One 4px corner (3px on small marks). No pills, no circles on containers.",
      "Flat. No cast shadows, gradients or glass, including the scrim and the pinned bars.",
      "The primary action is a full-width ink bar."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Field, Not Sprinkle Rule",
        "body": "A domain colour appears as a whole field, a full-height band square, or a solid rule (3px marker or timer edge). It never sets body text on the ground. Words on the ground use the matching text-safe tone.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Navy Ink Rule",
        "body": "Ink is navy, never #000. Anything drawn on a domain field, including chart lines, goal lines and axis labels, uses the on-field navy in both themes.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Own Domain Rule",
        "body": "Each domain colour belongs to its domain. Orange is nutrition only; a session in progress is training and stays sky. The one standing borrow is the PR badge, a solid Activity Yellow field with navy ink. Do not take a domain colour for decoration elsewhere.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Axis Grid Rule",
        "body": "Use one family and three widths: wide (112%) for headings, condensed (78%) for big numerals, and normal for reading. Do not introduce a second family. The one exception is the monospace account ID.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Still Numeral Rule",
        "body": "Numerals are tabular and never animate, count up or bounce. A changed value simply appears.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Full-Width Band Rule",
        "body": "Domain content is laid out as full-width stacked bands and fields, not a grid of floating cards. On desktop the grid is two columns, never a mosaic.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Field Rule",
        "body": "Never use a cast shadow, glow, gradient or backdrop blur on a redesigned surface. To lift something, step its tone or give it a rule.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Corner Rule",
        "body": "Use 4px, or 3px on small marks. No container or action is a pill or a circle. The Start action is a square, not a disc. Round forms belong only to the objects themselves: a pictogram's head, a plate, a wheel.",
        "section": "shapes"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** fill whole regions with a domain colour (a field, a band square or a 3px rule) and set navy ink on it in both themes.",
      "**Do** put a field's one action in a full-bleed ink bar at its foot, 56px tall.",
      "**Do** set headings and routine names wide, big numbers condensed and tabular, and reading text at normal width, all in Archivo.",
      "**Do** keep every corner at 4px, or 3px on small marks.",
      "**Do** separate surfaces with silver tone steps and 1px hairlines in the rule colour.",
      "**Do** use the text-safe tone (sky-text, green-text, orange-text, signal-red) for words and thin strokes on the ground.",
      "**Do** keep motion straight and ease-out (cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1)): 140ms for press feedback, 230–240ms for fields and controls. Honour reduced motion by removing it. The one travelling move is the `field` transition from a Home band into its screen's top field."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use #000 or any pure black for ink, text or the go bar.",
      "**Don't** add cast shadows, glows, gradients or backdrop blur to a surface. Lift it by tone or a rule instead.",
      "**Don't** make containers or actions into pills or circles. Use the square Start action and the square today marker.",
      "**Don't** set body text in a domain field colour on the white ground.",
      "**Don't** use Nutrition Orange outside nutrition. A session in progress is sky, marked by the ink bar on the Start square.",
      "**Don't** borrow a domain colour for decoration. The PR badge's yellow field is the one standing exception.",
      "**Don't** draw sport pictograms with square caps or interface icons with round ones. Figures are round-capped bars with a solid head; interface icons are square-capped strokes.",
      "**Don't** add a second typeface or fake widths with letter-spacing. Use the `wdth` axis.",
      "**Don't** animate numerals (no count-ups, no bounces).",
      "**Don't** add uppercase labels above headings. Uppercase is limited to a routine's name in a field, section labels over grouped lists, Stats tile labels, Plan's day squares and the weekday initials in the week strip."
    ]
  }
}
